 render_review strictly fills the shipped reviewer template with the work-item specification, lane range, test command, scratch location, optional review rubric and verdict destination; render_critique strictly fills the shipped critique template with the work-item specification and named rubric. Both refuse a missing specification, unreadable or empty named input, or unfilled template slot before a brief is written. review_refusal accepts only a verdict bound to the reviewed full commit with exactly one VERDICT line whose findings count matches its finding lines and whose changes request names a finding. round_path chooses the next ordinal lane round filename, file_review writes only an accepted verdict as that round record, and lane_commits resolves commits on a branch and requires the base to be an ancestor of the reviewed commit.\"","+rationale = \"An attended reviewer needs the same reviewed instructions and durable verdict carrier as an unattended review without inheriting its scheduler. Strict rendering and boundary validation prevent a reviewer from receiving incomplete instructions or an unrelated verdict from becoming review history.\"","+test_refs = \"TC-333\"","+status = \"Approved\"","+component = \"CMP-008\"","+phase = 6"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-852\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1827,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1827,"newLines":7,"lines":[" acceptance_criteria = \"An attended verdict bound to the reviewed commit and carrying one complete verdict line whose declared finding count matches its finding lines is recorded as the next ordinal review-round record and appears in the review rollup; a verdict that is unbound, malformed or count-mismatched is refused with no record.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," delivered_with = [\"SR-154\", \"SR-184\"]"," form = \"interface\""]}]},{"filePath":